Package: sessionsifu
Version: 3.5.11
Section: gnome
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Tomas Pluharik <tpluharik@gmail.com>
Depends: gjs, gnome-settings-daemon-common, python3, python3-gi, python3-pyatspi, python3-cryptography, python3-keyring, python3-pil, tesseract-ocr, gir1.2-gtk-4.0, gir1.2-adw-1, gir1.2-gdkpixbuf-2.0, gir1.2-gtop-2.0, procps, libglib2.0-bin, openssl
Recommends: gnome-shell, gnome-shell-extension-manager | gnome-shell-extension-prefs
Suggests: ydotool
Description: save and restore GNOME desktop layouts
 SessionSifu records running applications and window state, then relaunches
 applications and reconstructs their workspaces, monitors, geometry and state.
 It includes rolling automatic snapshots, recent-document restoration, a
  GNOME Shell 50 full-integration backend, GTK 4 manager, top-bar indicator and
  verified user-local updates. The manager and portable-safe functions install
  on Ubuntu 24.04/GNOME 46; full shell integration activates on GNOME 50.
  Companion portable builds support KDE Plasma, general GNOME, Windows and macOS.
